# auto-hide apps to scratchpad on launch
# NOTE: do NOT add a bare `move scratchpad` rule for whatsapp here. It would run
# before the instance rule below, and `resize set N ppt` / `move position center`
# are silent no-ops once a window is already in __i3_scratch (i3 reports success
# but the percentage resolves against the scratchpad pseudo-workspace). The
# window then keeps whatever geometry chrome restored, which is why it used to
# come back half-tiled instead of floating and centred. Size first, hide last.
for_window [class="TelegramDesktop" title="^Telegram"] move scratchpad
# bluebubbles: starts hidden and $mod+y toggles it, so hiding never kills
# the process and iMessage notifications keep working
# bluebubbles/whatsapp size is forced: bluebubbles does not persist window
# geometry on linux (its window-width/height prefs stay 1280x720 forever), and
# chrome app windows do not either. 60ppt = 60% of the monitor per axis, so this
# scales per machine. Fires on window creation only.
for_window [class="(?i)^bluebubbles$"] floating enable, resize set 60 ppt 60 ppt, move position center, move scratchpad
for_window [instance="(?i)^web\.whatsapp\.com$"] floating enable, resize set 60 ppt 60 ppt, move position center, move scratchpad
# firstmate ($mod+Shift+i): same 60ppt centred overlay as the two above, and the
# same mutual exclusion -- showing any one of the three hides the other two.
# "firstmate" is a WM_CLASS override passed to alacritty at launch, so this
# matches only that terminal and never an ordinary one.
#
# NOTE the deliberate absence of "move scratchpad" here. The other two are up
# from login to logout, so their toggle scripts never really have to launch
# anything and it does not matter that this rule would hide a fresh window.
# firstmate is a terminal the user quits often, so its toggle DOES have to launch
# and show -- with "move scratchpad" on this line that launch would be swallowed
# and the keypress would look dead. Hiding at login is done once, explicitly, by
# start_firstmate_hidden.sh instead.
for_window [class="(?i)^firstmate$"] floating enable, resize set 60 ppt 60 ppt, move position center
# spotify ($mod+Shift+s): same 60ppt centred overlay, and the same mutual
# exclusion -- showing any one of the four hides the other three.
#
# No "move scratchpad" here for the same reason as firstmate above: the toggle's
# "not running" branch has to launch AND SHOW, and this rule fires on every
# window creation including that one, so hiding here would swallow the launch and
# make the keypress look dead. Spotify IS pre-warmed at login, but the hiding for
# that is done once, explicitly, by start_spotify_hidden.sh -- not from here.
#
# VERIFIED 2026-07-29 with xprop on main's already-running client: WM_CLASS is
# "spotify", "Spotify". i3 matches [class=...] against the second field, so the
# capital S is what is actually being matched here. Kept case-insensitive on
# purpose -- the casing has moved between releases, and "(?i)^spotify$" is
# correct either way.
for_window [class="(?i)^spotify$"] floating enable, resize set 60 ppt 60 ppt, move position center

